2026-02-01 16:52:04 | INFO | "./webui\batch_video_generator.py:154": generate_single_video - Task completed successfully: {'videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\31519663-9f48-4b4e-81df-f44a50bf5efb\\final-1.mp4'], 'combined_videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\31519663-9f48-4b4e-81df-f44a50bf5efb\\combined-1.mp4'], 'script': "Stop right there! If you're reaching for plain tap water to thin out your Korean pancake batter, you are making a colossal, flavor-destroying mistake that will absolutely ruin the texture and ultimate enjoyment of your meal. Water drastically dilutes the crucial starch and protein ratio, which is essential for achieving that sought-after crispy, golden-brown crust, leaving you with a dishearteningly flimsy, rubbery, and utterly unappetizing pancake. Instead of a delightful crunch, your jeon will become a soggy, oil-logged mess, lacking the signature structural integrity and the irresistible textural contrast that defines a truly great Korean pancake. You’ll be left with a sad, limp disc that falls apart and absorbs excess grease, missing out entirely on the glorious, shatteringly crisp exterior that is the hallmark of authentic Korean jeon. The real secret to an incredibly crispy, non-soggy Korean pancake actually lies in using very cold liquid, specifically ice-cold water or, for an even deeper flavor profile, a light, chilled anchovy or vegetable broth. Using cold liquid significantly inhibits gluten development in the flour, preventing your batter from becoming chewy and bread-like and instead encouraging a light, airy, and ultimately crispier structure when it hits the hot pan. Furthermore, broth doesn't just add a fantastic layer of umami depth that plain water completely lacks; its subtle gelatin content also contributes to a more robust, satisfying texture that still manages to remain delicate and not heavy. This crucial swap ensures your pancake fries up beautifully, developing that perfect golden hue and a superior crunch that holds up without becoming tough. Imagine biting into a Korean pancake where the exterior is unbelievably golden and shatteringly crisp, giving way to a tender, perfectly cooked interior bursting with the fresh flavors of your chosen vegetables and seafood. Each and every bite will deliver that immensely satisfying crunch, a textural symphony that water-laden pancakes could only ever dream of achieving, transforming a simple meal into an extraordinary culinary experience. By ditching the tap water and embracing the power of cold liquid or savory broth, you’ll elevate your homemade jeon from merely good to absolutely legendary, impressing everyone at your table with its authentic taste and flawless texture. So next time you’re whipping up a batch of Korean pancakes, remember this crucial tip and prepare for the ultimate crispy, flavorful delight – your taste buds will undeniably thank you for it!", 'terms': ['soggy pancake', 'pancake batter', 'plain water', 'sparkling water', 'crispy pancake'], 'audio_file': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\31519663-9f48-4b4e-81df-f44a50bf5efb\\audio.mp3', 'audio_duration': 171, 'subtitle_path': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\31519663-9f48-4b4e-81df-f44a50bf5efb\\subtitle.srt', 'materials': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-803c6ec64c8f7d56d40e47a67760a18b.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-a4c8e8b3cef01705dc0ba2507672136b.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-f0b5fb3573d7d383c2deae9dcaa1dd70.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-467d2a3410a94b5c5156d5438cb22188.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-684eb3db7ddcf33a4e72b5f9b3eb89e6.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-9b5704ce64630110ae62cebc9a82bc67.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-72391ea98d09232231ea363cec49b68f.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtub