2026-02-01 20:52:44 | INFO | "./webui\batch_video_generator.py:246": generate_single_video - Returning successful result: {'file_path': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\30539020-79e0-4376-8ffd-3f2ce2cc85bc\\final-1.mp4', 'script': "The real secret to making healthy, unbelievably delicious ramen isn't a complex recipe; it's about intelligent ingredient swaps and embracing fresh, vibrant flavors that genuinely nourish your body. Forget the instant packets loaded with sodium and artificial ingredients; instead, build your foundation with a rich, low-sodium broth like homemade dashi, chicken bone broth, or a hearty vegetable stock, creating a depth of flavor that instantly elevates your bowl. Choose your noodles wisely, opting for whole wheat, soba, or even zucchini noodles to boost fiber and reduce refined carbohydrates, transforming your quick meal into a truly wholesome and satisfying experience without any guilt. This foundational shift is where the magic begins, setting the stage for a ramen that tastes incredible and makes you feel fantastic. Next, flood your ramen with a rainbow of nutrient-dense vegetables and lean proteins that pack a powerful punch of vitamins and minerals. Think crisp bok choy, tender spinach, earthy shiitake mushrooms, and vibrant shredded carrots, all simmered just enough to retain their delightful crunch and preserve their vital nutrients. For protein, perfectly soft-boiled eggs, thinly sliced grilled chicken breast, or firm tofu cubes absorb the beautiful broth flavors, ensuring every bite is packed with energy-sustaining goodness. These additions not only make your ramen incredibly flavorful and visually appealing, but they also transform it into a complete, balanced meal that will leave you feeling energized and deeply satisfied, a far cry from the post-instant-ramen slump. Finally, elevate your healthy ramen masterpiece with strategic flavor boosters and thoughtful garnishes that take it from good to absolutely unforgettable. A dollop of white miso paste stirred in at the end introduces a probiotic rich, umami depth, while a generous dash of fresh grated ginger and garlic provides an invigorating warmth and powerful anti-inflammatory benefits. Don't forget a drizzle of sesame oil for nutty aroma, a sprinkle of toasted sesame seeds for satisfying crunch, and a handful of fresh green onions or cilantro for a burst of freshness that brightens every spoonful. This isn't just about eating healthy; it’s about indulging in a ramen experience so incredibly flavorful, vibrant, and deeply satisfying, you'll wonder why you ever settled for anything less, proving that healthy can be utterly irresistible.", 'video_id': None, 'type': 'shorts', 'language': 'en-US', 'upload_error': None, 'file_size': 187129137, 'auto_upload_requested': True}
